# If you use Bossify in academic work or a derived product, please cite it.
# GitHub uses this file for the "Cite this repository" button.
# Replace given-names / family-names with the byline you will use on the paper
# before you post a preprint. Until a paper DOI exists, cite the software.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Bossify
message: If you use Bossify, please cite it using these metadata.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-01"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/chinaharry/bossify-with-claude"
url: "https://github.com/chinaharry/bossify-with-claude"
abstract: >-
  Local-first flight recorder and ROI analyzer for agentic coding sessions.
  Bossify attributes billed tokens to durable software outcomes from lossless
  session event logs (Claude Code, Cursor, Aider, and similar tools).
keywords:
  - agentic software engineering
  - token attribution
  - ROI
  - Claude Code
  - developer productivity measurement
authors:
  - family-names: chinaharry
    website: "https://github.com/chinaharry"
    affiliation: "School of Computer Science, The University of Sydney"
